        "original_id": "6a799968-8b0b-5beb-86a7-ff3c673fb8f9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Manhattan, New York City, Madison Avenue, East 23rd Street, Madison Square Park, Chelsea, Hell's Kitchen, Penn Station area, West Side Yards, Venice\n- Buildings: Metropolitan Life Insurance Company Tower, Met Life Tower, 15 Hudson Yards\n- Companies: Metropolitan Life Insurance Company, Hedden Construction Company, Metropolitan Transportation Authority\n- Organizations: Napoleon LeBrun & Sons\n- Projects: Hudson Yards project\n- Concepts: landmark skyscrapers, architectural design, urban redevelopment\n\nFacts:\n- The Metropolitan Life Insurance Company Tower, also called the Met Life Tower, is a landmark skyscraper on Madison Avenue at East 23rd Street across from Madison Square Park in Manhattan, New York City.\n- Napoleon LeBrun & Sons designed the Metropolitan Life Insurance Company Tower, and the Hedden Construction Company built it.\n- The Metropolitan Life Insurance Company Tower was modeled after the Campanile in Venice, Italy.\n- 15 Hudson Yards is located in Chelsea near the Hell's Kitchen Penn Station area.\n- 15 Hudson Yards is part of the Hudson Yards project.\n- The Hudson Yards project is a plan to redevelop the Metropolitan Transportation Authority's West Side Yards.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
